how. Looking at my hand, W7 is a single tile with no adjacent numbers. Similarly, B6 is in the middle but no adjacent tiles. \n\nBetween W7 and B6, which is safer? \n\nIf I discard W7, there's no W6 or W8 in my hand. If someone has W6 or W8, they might take it. But I don't have them. \n\nIf I discard B6, someone with B5 or B7 could take it. I have B7. \n\nBut since I have B7, if someone has B5, they could chi B5-B6-B7. \n\nBut B5 has 4 left. So possible. \n\nBut if I discard B6, it's possible someone takes it. \n\nIf I discard W7, less chance. \n\nSo maybe discard W7. \n\nLooking at the valid actions, W7 is an option. \n\nSo the answer would be Play W7.\n", "output": "Evaluation: [Discarding W7 to avoid potential chow opportunities for others and maintain concealed hand flexibility.]\nReason: [W7 is a single tile not part of any pung or chow in the current hand. Discarding it minimizes the risk of aiding opponents in forming melds, while preserving pairs (W2, B3) and concealed hand points. Other options like B3 or W2 involve pairs that could lead to higher-value pungs if retained.]\nAnswer: Play W7"}
