"output": "Evaluation: The best move is to discard B6 to avoid losing potential chows in the Dot suit while maintaining flexibility for future melds.\nReason: Discarding B6, which is part of a less critical sequence (B5-B6-B7) and has multiple remaining tiles in the wall, minimizes the risk of aiding opponents. Keeping T1-T6 in Dots allows for forming two chows (T1-T2-T3 and T4-T5-T6) and preserves B3 pairs for possible pungs.\nAnswer: Play B6"}
